<article class="env-lemma" id="0BYJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BYJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0BYJ">15.60.15</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K^\bullet , L^\bullet , M^\bullet $ be complexes of $R$-modules. There is a canonical isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (K^\bullet \otimes _ R^\mathbf {L} L^\bullet ) \otimes _ R^\mathbf {L} M^\bullet = K^\bullet \otimes _ R^\mathbf {L} (L^\bullet \otimes _ R^\mathbf {L} M^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> functorial in all three complexes. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Replace the complexes by K-flat complexes and use the associativity constraint in Section <a href="/tag/0GWN" data-tag="0GWN">15.59</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>